{{also|Trammel}}
==English==
[[File:Llares.png|thumb|trammel rings (4) used to hang cooking pots]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|trameyle}}, from {{der|en|fro|tramail||net for catching fish}}, from {{der|en|LL.|tremaculum}}. See {{der|en|it|tramaglio}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtræməl/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-trammel.wav|Audio (RP)}}
* {{rhymes|en|æməl|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Whatever [[impede]]s activity, progress, or freedom, such as a net or [[shackle]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1825|author={{w|Francis Jeffrey|author2=Lord Jeffrey|Francis Jeffrey}}|chapter=Campbell's Theodric|title={{w|The Edinburgh Review}} January 1825
|passage=[They] disclaim the '''trammels''' of any sordid contract.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1898|year_published=1911|author=[[s:Author:William Graham Sumner|William Graham Sumner]]|title=[[s:War and Other Essays|War and Other Essays]]|chapter=[[s:The Conquest of the United States by Spain|The Conquest of the United States by Spain]]|publisher=Yale|page=[[s:Page:War and Other Essays.djvu/368|332]]|passage=The men who came here were able to throw off all the '''trammels''' of tradition and established doctrine.}}
# A [[fishing]] [[net]] that has large [[mesh]] at the edges and smaller mesh in the middle
# A kind of net for catching birds, fishes, or other prey.
#* '''1633''', {{RQ:Carew Survey of Cornwall}}
#*:The tuck carrieth a like fashion , save that it is narrower meshed , and ( therefore scarce lawful ) with a long bunt in the midst : the '''trammel''' differeth not much from the shape of this bunt, and serveth to such use as the wear and haking.
# A set of [[ring]]s or other hanging devices, attached to a [[transverse]] bar suspended over a [[fire]], used to hang [[cooking pot]]s etc.
# A net for confining a woman's hair.
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|2|2|passage=Her golden lockes she roundly did uptye <br>In breaded '''tramels''', that no looser heares <br>Did out of order stray about her daintie eares.}}
# A kind of shackle used for regulating the motions of a horse and making it [[amble]].
# {{lb|en|engineering}} An instrument for drawing [[ellipsis|ellipses]], one part of which consists of a cross with two grooves at right angles to each other, the other being a [[beam]] carrying two pins (which slide in those grooves), and also the [[describe|describing]] pencil.
# A [[beam compass]].

