===Verb===
{{en-verb|++|pres_ptc_qual=UK|pres_ptc2=trammeling|pres_ptc2_qual=US|past_qual=UK|past2=trammeled|past2_qual=US}}

# To [[entangle]], as in a [[net]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1880|author=[[w:Dante Gabriel Rosetti|Dante Gabriel Rosetti]]|title=Samuel Taylor Coleridge|lines=9-10
|passage=the scarce-snatched hours<br>Which deepening pain left to his lordliest powers: —<br>Heaven lost through spider-'''trammelled''' prison-bars.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[confine]]; to [[hamper]]; to [[shackle]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1854|author=Henry David Thoreau|title=Slavery in Massachusetts|passage=In their vote, you would get something of some value, at least, however small; but in the other case, only the '''trammelled''' judgment of an individual, of no significance, be it which way it might.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1948|author=Winston Churchill|title=[[w:The Second World War (book series)|The Second World War]]|passage=Virtuous motives, '''trammeled''' by inertia and timidity, are no match for armed and resolute wickedness.}}

